Three errors:

1. `SelectionCheckbox` not exported from package root? But `components/index.d.ts` has `export * from "./SelectionCheckbox/index.js"` and root index.d.ts exports named list from components/index.js — wait, the root index.d.ts I read earlier had an explicit named export list: `export { BaseTable, ReorderingProvider, ..., RangedSelectionCheckbox } from "./components/index.js";` — SelectionCheckbox is NOT in that named list! It's exported from components/index.d.ts via `export *`, but root re-exports only named ones. So `SelectionCheckbox` isn't available from root. Options: use `RangedSelectionCheckbox` (exported) — but ranged is undefined with nesting. Or check for a subpath export... exports keys: ".", "./tanstack", "./tanstack-virtual". No components subpath. So SelectionCheckbox is unreachable.

Alternative: build the checkbox cell with uikit's `Checkbox` directly (the docs' custom ranged example imports Checkbox from uikit). So:

```tsx
import {Checkbox} from '@gravity-ui/uikit';

const groupedSelectionColumn: ColumnDef<OrderTableItem> = {
  id: '_select',
  header: ({table}) => (
    <Checkbox
      size="l"
      checked={table.getIsAllRowsSelected()}
      disabled={!table.options.enableRowSelection}
      indeterminate={table.getIsSomeRowsSelected()}
      onChange={table.getToggleAllRowsSelectedHandler()}
    />
  ),
  cell: ({row}) => (
    <Checkbox
      size="l"
      checked={row.getIsSelected()}
      disabled={!row.getCanSelect()}
      indeterminate={row.getIsSomeSelected()}
      onChange={row.getToggleSelectedHandler()}
    />
  ),
  ...
};
```

Checkbox uikit props: checked, indeterminate, disabled, onChange, size — long-standing API. The docs example itself uses exactly this with uikit Checkbox (lines 122, 147-162 of INDEX.md). 

2. `enableColumnReordering` doesn't exist on ColumnDef<OrderTableItem> — because I imported ColumnDef from '@gravity-ui/table/tanstack' which re-exports TanStack's own ColumnDef, NOT the extended @gravity-ui/table one with withNestingStyles/enableColumnReordering! Recall types/base.d.ts: `export type ColumnDef<TData, TValue> = BaseColumnDef & {withNestingStyles?...; enableColumnReordering?...}`. That extended ColumnDef is exported from root: `export type * from "./types/base.js"`. So import ColumnDef from '@gravity-ui/table' (root), not from /tanstack. The docs said types like RowSelectionState/SortingState come from /tanstack — those are TanStack state types. ColumnDef should come from root to get the extensions. In the docs' basic example they import ColumnDef from '/tanstack' — that works for plain columns but not for the extended flags.

Fix: `import type {ColumnDef} from '@gravity-ui/table';` and keep ExpandedState, RowSelectionState from '/tanstack'.

Wait — does the root export ColumnDef? `export type * from "./types/base.js"` — yes, ColumnDef is in types/base.d.ts. But root index.d.ts also exports types from tanstack? No. And does root ColumnDef conflict with anything? Fine.

But `useTable` options expect `columns: ColumnDef<TData, any>[]` from its own types/base — the same extended type. 

Also 'size' etc. remain TanStack props, included in BaseColumnDef. Good.

Let me fix both.

